  "id": "Compound::DB01110 - Gene::27345",
  "verbalization": "Miconazole appears to interact with Kcnmb4 through a shared pathway involving Ca-activated K+ channels. The evidence suggests that Miconazole binds to Kcnn1, Kcnn3, or Kcnmb3, all of which participate in the regulation of Ca-activated K+ channels. These channels are then implicated in the participation of Kcnmb4, indicating a potential functional link between Miconazole and Kcnmb4. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific target of Miconazole—whether Kcnn1, Kcnn3, or Kcnmb3—is not definitively resolved. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of Ca-activated K+ channels, which in turn may influence Kcnmb4's function. This integrated pathway highlights the role of Kcnmb4 in the regulation of Ca-activated K+ channels, possibly through interactions with these channels, and underscores the importance of Kcnmb4 in cellular processes involving ion channel regulation.",
